TEXT -2000 1200 Left 2 ;.ac dec 1k 1 10Meg
TEXT -208 2488 Left 3 ;Step 0. Ensure all voltage references and bias voltages are correct.\n \nStep 1. Reflect/Reference diode on control output winding to primary side. Leave other diodes remaining to emulate loss.\n \nStep 2. Set turns ratio parameter of averaged switch/diode circuit to 1\n \nStep 3. Configure peak-current sense block correctly.\nVL_P = Most positive voltage of magnetizing inductor when switch is ON (+VIN for this flyback)\nVL_N = Most negative voltage of magnetizing inductor when switch is ON (GND for this flyback)\nV_ILAvg = Averaged magnetizing inductor current when switch is ON, which is equal to the average switch current\n \nStep 4. Use high-gain voltage amp to drive feedback such that EA_OUT = Scaled peak current sense,\nwhich equates to peak current mode control.\n \nStep 5. Wire external compensator/feedback.
TEXT 120 -264 Left 2 !.param L_AB = 9.53u\n.param L_21 = 22.0u\n.param L_43 = 22.3u\n.param L_56 = 22.3u\n.param L_78 = 2.50u\n.param L_9_10 = 9.03u
